OL,3,GNEWSAAnti-social behaviour rising in
OL,4,Ahousing, finds report
OL,5,
OL,6,FBrighton and Hove City Council's (BHCC)
OL,7,Fhousing team dealt with more than 900
OL,8,Freports of anti-social behaviour last
OL,9,Fyear, 13% more than the previous year,
OL,10,Faccording to a new report.
OL,12,FOf the 920 reports, 30 included hate
OL,13,Fincidents, BHCC's People Overview and
OL,14,FScrutiny Committee were told in a
OL,15,Fmeeting last week.
OL,17,FHarry Williams, BHCC's director of
OL,18,Fhousing people services, said the
OL,19,Fcouncil recognised the need to do more
OL,20,Faround support for people.
OL,23,APub: 15-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
